diff --git a/docs/inventory-screen.md b/docs/inventory-screen.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9268d5b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/inventory-screen.md
@@ -0,0 +1,125 @@
+# Inventory screen
+
+The block inventory lets a player see every block type, how many they have, which ones are locked
+and at what level they unlock, and pick the block to build with.
+
+Code: `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/UI/` (`InventoryScreen` wires it to the game;
+`Components/` holds the view; stories are in `src/ServerScriptService/Stories/Inventory`).
+
+## Who and when
+
+- **Player:** mostly children aged about 6 to 12. Short words, one-line messages, big targets.
+- **Device designed first:** a phone held sideways. It also has to work on tablet, PC, and Xbox.
+- **Moment:** in the middle of building. The player opens the screen, picks a block, and gets
+  back to building. Picking should take one press after opening.
+
+## What's on screen
+
+| Element | Job | When it shows |
+|---|---|---|
+| Blocks button (HUD) | Opens the panel. Shows the color and name of the block in use | Always |
+| Backdrop | Dims the world. Tapping it closes the panel | While open |
+| Panel header | "Blocks" title, the player's level, a status line, and a close button | While open |
+| Block tile (x10) | One per block type: color swatch, name, then count (`x48`) or lock and `Level 6` | While open |
+
+Every block type is always shown, locked ones included, so players can see what's coming.
+
+### Tile states
+
+| State | What the player sees (always more than just a color) |
+|---|---|
+| Normal | Swatch, name, `x<count>` |
+| Empty (0) | Same, with `x0` in muted text. The tile can still be picked |
+| Locked | Darker tile, faded swatch with a **padlock**, `Level <n>` in place of the count |
+| In use | Gold border **and** a gold `Using` tag on top of the tile |
+| Hover (mouse) | Tile gets lighter |
+| Focused (controller or keyboard) | White ring around the tile, separate from the gold "in use" border |
+| Pressed | Tile shrinks to 94% and springs back. Locked tiles also shake side to side |
+
+Counts at 1,000 or more read like `1.2K` or `12M`, so the label stays the same width.
+
+## Where it sits
+
+| | Blocks button | Panel |
+|---|---|---|
+| Phone (touch) | Right edge, halfway down, 12 from the edge | Centered. Compact layout: 96x102 tiles |
+| Tablet (touch) | Right edge, 60% down, above the jump button | Centered. Regular layout: 104x120 tiles |
+| PC | Bottom middle | Centered. Regular layout |
+| Xbox / TV | Bottom middle | Centered. Regular layout, whole UI scaled 1.25x |
+
+- Nothing goes in the bottom corners on touch (the thumbstick and jump button live there) or
+  under the Roblox top bar (the ScreenGui uses `CoreUISafeInsets`).
+- The layout follows `UserInputService.PreferredInput` and the live screen size, so plugging in a
+  controller or rotating a device switches it on the spot.
+- The panel shrinks to fit small screens (never below half size). On a 667x375 phone the compact
+  panel draws at about 98%.
+
+## Opening and closing
+
+| Action | Touch | Mouse and keyboard | Controller |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Open | Tap the Blocks button | Click the Blocks button, or press **B** (a `B` key badge shows on the button) | Press **Y** (its glyph shows on the button), or select the Blocks button and press **A** |
+| Close | Tap the **X**, tap the dimmed area outside the panel, or pick a block | Click the **X** or outside the panel, press **B** again, or pick a block | Press **B**, press **Y** again, select the **X** and press **A**, or pick a block |
+
+- When the panel is opened by key or controller, focus starts on the tile of the block in use.
+  When it closes, focus goes back to whatever was selected before (usually nothing, so the
+  controller drives the character again).
+- Controller focus can't leave the panel while it's open (`SelectionGroup` set to `Stop`).
+- While the panel is open, Roblox's touch thumbstick and jump button are hidden, and taps and
+  clicks in the world don't place blocks. Both come back when it closes.
+- Opening: the panel slides up 24 units and the backdrop fades in (spring period 0.25 s). Closing
+  is instant. With **Reduced Motion** on, the panel appears in place with no slide.
+
+## Picking a block
+
+| Action | Touch | Mouse and keyboard | Controller |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Pick an unlocked block | Tap its tile | Click its tile, or press its number key (**1** to **9**, **0**; shown in the tile's corner) | Move with the D-pad or left stick, press **A** |
+| Find out why a block is locked | Tap it | Click it | Focus it and press **A** |
+
+- Picking a block makes it the one in use (`BlockPlacer.setBlockType`) and closes the panel. That's
+  one press from open to building again.
+- Pressing a locked tile doesn't pick it. The tile shakes and the status line says
+  "Ice unlocks at level 4". The tile already shows `Level 4` and a lock, so nothing is
+  hover-only.
+- Number keys skip locked blocks (`BlockPlacer` now checks `BlockInventory.isUnlocked`), so the
+  keyboard can't pick a block the panel shows as locked.
+- Counts, locks, and the level update live while the panel is open (`BlockInventory.Changed`).
+
+## Accessibility
+
+- Text is Builder Sans in fixed sizes (title 30, names 20, counts 18, captions 16 at 1080p), so it
+  follows the player's Roblox text size setting. TV text is 1.25x bigger.
+- Text and key icons are at least 4.5:1 against their tile. Locked text is about 6.5:1.
+- Locked and in-use states always have a shape or word next to the color: padlock plus `Level n`;
+  border plus `Using`.
+- Backgrounds follow the player's **Background Transparency** setting, and motion follows
+  **Reduced Motion**.
+- Every target is at least 44 UI units: tiles are 96 or more, the close button is 44 to 52, and
+  the Blocks button is 88.
+
+**Known exception:** at the Largest text size, long names may get cut off with `...` in their
+fixed-width tiles. The status line wraps. This hasn't been checked in Studio yet.
+
+## Open questions to playtest
+
+1. Does picking a block and closing in one press feel right, or do kids want the panel to stay
+   open to compare? Watch about five new players. Count how often they reopen the panel right
+   after picking.
+2. Do kids find the Blocks button on a phone at the right edge, halfway down, without being told?
+   Log `inventory_opened` with the input type, and the time from joining to the first open.
+3. Do players understand `Level 4` on a locked tile without pressing it? Log `locked_tile_pressed`
+   with the block name.
+4. Should a block with 0 count be pickable? Right now it is, and the server doesn't check counts
+   yet.
+
+## Not verified yet
+
+These need Studio, which this change couldn't reach:
+
+- Whether the Roblox B button runs after our high-priority `CloseBlockInventory` binding. Test in
+  the Controller Emulator.
+- Whether arrow keys and Enter move between tiles and pick on keyboard once focus is set. The
+  number keys are the guaranteed keyboard path.
+- How the layout looks in the Device Emulator: small phone, short phone, tablet, 1080p, 1440p, and
+  Xbox, at Largest text size.
